  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ajay Kumar Agarwal vs State Of U.P. on 21 April, 2025 Author: Ashutosh Srivastava Bench: Ashutosh Srivastava High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Neutral Citation No. - 2025:Ahc:58241 Court No. - 68 Case :- Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 2308 of 2025 Applicant :- Ajay Kumar Agarwal",
    "facts": "This bail application under Section 483 of Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 has been moved on behalf of accused-applicant, Ajay Kumar Agarwal, seeking enlargement on bail in Case Crime No. 473 of 2024, under 274, 275 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 and Section 26 (2), (1) (4), 59 (1) of the Food Safety & Standard Act, 2006, Police Station Khurja Dehat, District Bulandshahr.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant argued that the accused-applicant is innocent. He has been falsely implicated in this very case crime number and is languishing in jail since 6.12.2024. 1 counsel for the applicant submits that the allegation against the applicant is that he was selling the raw material to the co-accused persons for manufacturing the alleged diary products. Learned counsel for the applicant submits that the maximum punishment in the aforesaid sections are punishable with six months and the applicant has already undergone period of more than five months. Co-accused Firoz Khan, has been granted bail by this Court, in Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. 8248 of 2025, vide order dated 09.04.2025. He has no criminal antecedent and there is no likelihood of his fleeing from course of justice or tampering with evidence in case of release on bail. Hence, bail has been prayed for. Learned AGA has vehemently opposed the prayer for bail.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant argued that the accused-applicant is innocent. He has been falsely implicated in this very case crime number and is languishing in jail since 6.12.2024. 1 counsel for the applicant submits that the allegation against the applicant is that he was selling the raw material to the co-accused persons for manufacturing the alleged diary products.",
    "respondent_arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant submits that the maximum punishment in the aforesaid sections are punishable with six months and the applicant has already undergone period of more than five months. Co-accused Firoz Khan, has been granted bail by this Court, in Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. 8248 of 2025, vide order dated 09.04.2025. He has no criminal antecedent and there is no likelihood of his fleeing from course of justice or tampering with evidence in case of release on bail. Hence, bail has been prayed for. Learned AGA has vehemently opposed the prayer for bail.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
